-- title:
--   Kronecker–Weyl equidistribution theorem — for $\mathbb Q$-independent $\tau$, time averages of $u(t\tau \bmod \mathbb Z^N)$ converge to $\int_{\mathbb T^N}u\,d\mu_N$
-- statement:
--   **The Kronecker–Weyl equidistribution theorem ($\mathbb Q$-independent frequencies).** Let $N\ge0$, $\mathbb T=\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$, and let $\mu_N$ be the Haar measure of total mass $1$ on the torus $\mathbb T^N$. Let $\tau=(\tau_1,\dots,\tau_N)\in\mathbb R^N$ have coordinates that are linearly independent over $\mathbb Q$, and let $\overline\gamma(t)=(t\tau_1,\dots,t\tau_N)\bmod\mathbb Z^N$ be the one-parameter subgroup of $\mathbb T^N$ generated by $\tau$. Then for every continuous function $u\colon\mathbb T^N\to\mathbb C$,
--   $$\lim_{T\to+\infty}\frac1{2T}\int_{-T}^{T}u(\overline\gamma(t))\,dt=\lim_{T\to+\infty}\frac1T\int_0^Tu(\overline\gamma(t))\,dt=\int_{\mathbb T^N}u(\xi)\,d\mu_N(\xi).$$
--
--   This is equation (B.5.2.1) of Theorem B.5.2.1(2) of the source in the case of $\mathbb Q$-linearly independent coordinates (where the orbit closure is $G=\mathbb T^N$ by part (1)) and of continuous $u$; the source states that this is the only case of the theorem it requires, and its proof reduces the general statement to it. It expresses the unique ergodicity of the linear flow $\xi\mapsto\xi+\overline\gamma(t)$ on $\mathbb T^N$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The index set $\{1,\dots,N\}$ is an arbitrary finite type `ι` (so $N=0$ is allowed). $\mathbb T$ is Mathlib's `UnitAddCircle = AddCircle (1 : ℝ)`, the coercion `ℝ → UnitAddCircle` is the quotient map $\mathbb R\to\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$, and $\mathbb T^N$ is `ι → UnitAddCircle` (Mathlib's `UnitAddTorus ι`) with the product topology; $\overline\gamma_\tau(t)$ is written inline as `fun k => ((t * τ k : ℝ) : UnitAddCircle)`. $\mu_N$ is the `volume` of `UnitAddTorus ι`, the product of the Haar probability measures of the factors; $u$ is a bundled continuous map `C(UnitAddTorus ι, ℂ)`. The two limits are stated as a conjunction of two `Tendsto … atTop` statements, with the forward average $T^{-1}\int_0^T$ first.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 627, Theorem B.5.2.1(2) (Kronecker-Weyl), eq. (B.5.2.1), case of Q-linearly independent coordinates and continuous u; classical reference: B. Hasselblatt and A. Katok, A First Course in Dynamics. With a Panorama of Recent Developments, Cambridge University Press, 2003, Part 1, Theorem 4.1.15 and §4.1.6 (of which the source's theorem is the multi-dimensional version); P. Humphreys, The Summatory Function of Liouville's Function and Pólya's Conjecture, BPh thesis, Australian National University, 2010, §4.3, proof of Lemma 4.3 (general case, as cited by the source)

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory Filter Topology

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace KroneckerWeyl

theorem tendsto_average_torusFlow {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (τ : ι → ℝ)
    (hτ : LinearIndependent ℚ τ) (u : C(UnitAddTorus ι, ℂ)) :
    Tendsto (fun T : ℝ => T⁻¹ • ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..T, u fun k => ((t * τ k : ℝ) : UnitAddCircle))
        atTop (𝓝 (∫ ξ, u ξ)) ∧
      Tendsto
        (fun T : ℝ => (2 * T)⁻¹ • ∫ t in (-T)..T, u fun k => ((t * τ k : ℝ) : UnitAddCircle))
        atTop (𝓝 (∫ ξ, u ξ)) := by sorry

end KroneckerWeyl
